Z||000002||RedOktober||12-12-2000||11:30 PM||||its for the mazda 323 1.6L .. too small for your 2.8....unless you find a match.. and then we'll talk..( twin turbo) woooohhhooooo,<BR> The smallest you wanyt to run with the 2.8 is the IHI RHB5..<P>Try to find a good turbo from a wrecker.. about $50. and get it rebuilt. ($300-900).<P>good donor turbos... 2.2 Dodges... 2.3/5 ???from Ford, and or get a custom one.. T3/T4 Hybred.. ($700New.. in my area)<BR>good luck.<P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"||||reg||1
Z||000003||afRaceR||12-12-2000||11:45 PM||||Another good turbo is off of a Dodge Conquest or Mitsu Starion....same car. Although these are harder to find than fieros the turbo will work. The motors are 2.6 4cyl and there are two different sizes available stock. You want to find one that has a intercooler on it. These are a little bit bigger than the one without intercooler, plus you can yank the cooler while you're there. Plus there are lots of upgrades for these.<BR>I just happen to have one you can buy.....you just have to buy the whole car to get it though.||||reg||1
